WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
BILL: Here we are
in Overtime, uh...

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.101
-let's see.
-(APPLAUSE)

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:04.170
Oh, must have gone good tonight.

00:00:04.236 --> 00:00:08.041
Uh. Louie,
do you have any suggestions
for keeping a family together

00:00:08.274 --> 00:00:10.944
in this era
of hyper-partisan politics?

00:00:11.044 --> 00:00:13.646
Well, yeah,
you kind of bridge the divide.

00:00:13.779 --> 00:00:16.582
-You're a Mid-Western boy,
but you're a city slicker now.
-Yeah.

00:00:16.815 --> 00:00:19.118
I think-- You know, like,
I visit home.

00:00:19.318 --> 00:00:22.388
I go back to Minnesota
eight to ten times a year,

00:00:22.455 --> 00:00:24.357 line:0%
which is a lot,
but I work a lot there.

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:27.693 line:0%
But I always see my brothers
and sisters, all the time,

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:32.598 line:0%
and even the times
when we don't have time,
you gotta check in.

00:00:32.765 --> 00:00:35.534
And I think it's about
checking in and keeping people
part of your life.

00:00:35.601 --> 00:00:37.336
-And keep talking, right?
-Yeah.

00:00:37.403 --> 00:00:38.404
Not cut people off, that--

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:41.975
Keep talking.
And even if you're mad at them,
or they're mad at you,

00:00:42.242 --> 00:00:44.777
don't let them run away from you
and don't let them hide.

00:00:44.944 --> 00:00:47.380
Okay. Geraldo,
after all the work--

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:48.581
(APPLAUSE)

00:00:48.881 --> 00:00:51.417
...you did exposing
mental institutions,
like Willowbrook,

00:00:51.584 --> 00:00:55.588
what do you really think
about Trump declaring we need
to reopen these institutions.

00:00:55.655 --> 00:00:58.024
I think,
as Governor Spitzer knows,

00:00:58.090 --> 00:01:00.393 line:0%
there's a confusion
in the public mind,

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:02.395 line:0%
between people
who are mentally ill,

00:01:02.461 --> 00:01:09.101 line:0%
which includes schizophrenia,
post- traumatic stress,
you know, uh... bi-polar...

00:01:09.535 --> 00:01:14.907
That's different from my area,
which is the developmentally
disabled, mentally--

00:01:14.974 --> 00:01:16.442
They used to call them
"mentally retarded."

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:22.381
Down syndrome, autistic, uh...
People who were warehoused
in institutions.

00:01:22.448 --> 00:01:24.116
-BILL: Right.
-Not asylums,

00:01:24.216 --> 00:01:27.019
but they were warehouses
that existed, people forget.

00:01:27.086 --> 00:01:29.322
-Over five thousand people--
-The Kennedys put their...

00:01:29.889 --> 00:01:32.124
(STUTTERS) And lobotomy,
and all the rest of it.

00:01:32.191 --> 00:01:34.660
It was just horrible,
horrible treatment of--

00:01:34.894 --> 00:01:37.897
One has, kinda normal IQ
and there's something off,

00:01:37.964 --> 00:01:41.534
and those are the people
who are running down the street,
uh, with guns,

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:42.768
or things that look like guns.

00:01:43.202 --> 00:01:48.340
And then the developmentally
disabled are people whose IQs
are below normal,

00:01:48.474 --> 00:01:52.745
who you want to have as much
humane living environment
as possible.

00:01:52.879 --> 00:01:59.052
They're gentle people,
they're obviously very needy,
but they can be...

00:01:59.452 --> 00:02:02.021
you know...
(STUTTERS)

00:02:02.188 --> 00:02:05.257
...take vocational training,
they can evolve,
they can live longer,

00:02:05.491 --> 00:02:09.862
rather than be in institutions,
where 60 of them were jammed
in a room, naked,

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:14.500
smeared with their own feces,
unattended.
One attendant for 60 people.

00:02:14.967 --> 00:02:18.737
I'll ask one more
Trump thing then,
when he did that thing...

00:02:19.204 --> 00:02:20.339
-It was terrible.
-Okay.

00:02:20.405 --> 00:02:21.474
-It was terrible.
-Okay.

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:24.744
(LAUGHTER AND APPLAUSE)

00:02:24.844 --> 00:02:27.147
(BILL LAUGHS)

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:29.148
-HEATHER: Couldn't help it.
-Yeah, I couldn't help it.

00:02:29.248 --> 00:02:30.917
(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:02:30.983 --> 00:02:34.854
Um... Max, do you believe
the US has learned
from our experience in Vietnam--

00:02:34.954 --> 00:02:36.756
-Terrific book by the way.
-Thank you.

00:02:36.823 --> 00:02:39.124
-Great book. Great writer.
I recommend it highly.
-LOUIE: Congratulations.

00:02:39.224 --> 00:02:40.426
-(APPLAUSE)
-Uh...

00:02:40.693 --> 00:02:43.495
Do you believe that the US
has learned from our experience
in Vietnam,

00:02:43.629 --> 00:02:46.065
or that we are continuing to
make many of the same mistakes?

00:02:46.299 --> 00:02:50.002
Obviously, not in Vietnam,
but I assume this person
means somewhere else.

00:02:50.335 --> 00:02:53.072 line:0%
Uh. Unfortunately, I think
we continue to make a lot
of the same mistakes,

00:02:53.238 --> 00:02:56.242 line:0%
and this is a frustration
for me, as a historian.
You can study the history,

00:02:56.409 --> 00:03:00.146 line:0%
you can draw the lessons.
Getting people to actually
internalize them and act on them

00:03:00.279 --> 00:03:03.382 line:0%
is something else.
And for example, today,
across the Middle East,

00:03:03.582 --> 00:03:06.552
when we are fighting
the war on terrorism, I think
there is a tendency to think,

00:03:06.652 --> 00:03:08.054
especially on the part
of the president,

00:03:08.221 --> 00:03:10.590
that American bombs and bullets
will win the day.

00:03:10.723 --> 00:03:12.692
And there was a similar tendency
in Vietnam to think

00:03:12.859 --> 00:03:14.927
we could bomb the Viet Cong
into submission.

00:03:15.061 --> 00:03:18.598
General William Westmoreland
thought we could kill
the Viet Cong faster

00:03:18.664 --> 00:03:21.834
than they could be replaced.
And the guy that I wrote about,
Edward Lansdale said,

00:03:22.001 --> 00:03:24.236
"No, this is never going
to work out,
the only way to win

00:03:24.369 --> 00:03:25.705
is to have a viable instate,

00:03:25.805 --> 00:03:29.242
a government in South Vietnam
that the people
can actually support.

00:03:29.408 --> 00:03:32.011
And today, we're not really
focused on creating governments
that people can support

00:03:32.078 --> 00:03:35.281
across the Middle East,
we're just focused on bombing
and then leaving,

00:03:35.548 --> 00:03:37.850
and that's not gonna be
a successful long-term strategy.

00:03:38.016 --> 00:03:41.187
Yeah, I know he talks about ISIS
being annihilated, but...

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:46.225
they may be annihilated
in Syria, but they're just going
to take their talents to...

00:03:46.459 --> 00:03:47.460
LOUIE: South Beach.

00:03:47.594 --> 00:03:50.229
-Well, that's what I was...
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:03:50.462 --> 00:03:53.999
-But in their case,
Libya or Somalia...
-(OVERLAPPING CHATTER)

00:03:54.066 --> 00:03:55.401
No, that's what I was invoking.

00:03:55.468 --> 00:03:57.069
-(OVERLAPPING CHATTER)
-(BILL LAUGHS)

00:03:57.136 --> 00:03:58.671
Remember what happened
with Al-Qaeda in Iraq.

00:03:58.871 --> 00:04:03.109
Al-Qaeda in Iraq, which was
the predecessor of ISIS,
was annihilated by 2011.

00:04:03.242 --> 00:04:06.679
Then President Obama pulled
our troops out of Iraq,
a decision I opposed.

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:10.883
As a result of that,
he created breathing space
for ISIS to arise

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:13.619
and to take this vast caliphate
across Syria and Iraq.

00:04:13.719 --> 00:04:16.889
And my concern is that Trump
today, is going to repeat
that very same mistake,

00:04:16.955 --> 00:04:19.958
that he and other Republicans
were criticizing
not so long ago.

00:04:20.059 --> 00:04:22.628
-BILL: Do you think--
-LOUIE: Isn't it also true,
if I might say,

00:04:22.728 --> 00:04:26.366
that we always look at our model
as the model
for other countries,

00:04:26.432 --> 00:04:31.437
and we have no idea of all
these tribal things,
and all this history.

00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:35.274
And I think we always try
to get these people
to do things our way,

00:04:35.341 --> 00:04:37.410
and they don't have
what we have to do that.

00:04:37.477 --> 00:04:41.113
They define freedom differently.
I mean, that was
George Bush's big mistake.

00:04:41.213 --> 00:04:42.748
He was like,
"Everybody loves freedom!"

00:04:43.015 --> 00:04:46.352
We also forget
that it's all about religion
in the Middle East.

00:04:46.752 --> 00:04:50.056
We don't understand that
the Shiites are different
than the Sunnis.

00:04:50.156 --> 00:04:54.794
We changed the order,
and the Iraq invasion of '03,

00:04:55.227 --> 00:04:57.496
unsettled the society
that had settled,

00:04:57.763 --> 00:05:00.900
however maybe unfair
it could be perceived from...

00:05:01.567 --> 00:05:06.705
people in a democratic society.
But religion rules
in the Middle East.

00:05:06.772 --> 00:05:09.942
It's been forever, a millennium.
It'll be forever.

00:05:10.042 --> 00:05:13.813
And history that happened
600 years ago, to them,
is like yesterday.

00:05:13.946 --> 00:05:14.880
Yeah.

00:05:15.147 --> 00:05:16.682
That's not just the Middle East,
that's a lot of countries.

00:05:16.748 --> 00:05:19.085
Yugoslavia,
when that place fell apart.

00:05:19.285 --> 00:05:20.853
You've gotta have on-the-ground
understanding,

00:05:20.919 --> 00:05:22.621
like the guy I wrote about,
Ed Lansdale,

00:05:22.788 --> 00:05:24.690
who spent years
in the Philippines and Vietnam,

00:05:24.790 --> 00:05:26.626
and really came to understand
the society.

00:05:26.859 --> 00:05:28.894
And he was trying to talk
truth to power...

00:05:29.328 --> 00:05:32.031 line:0%
to generals who thought
they could just bomb
their way to victory.

00:05:32.198 --> 00:05:34.433 line:0%
But today, you know, I see,
unfortunately,
a similar mindset,

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:36.269 line:0%
where, again, there's not--
In the White House,

00:05:36.335 --> 00:05:37.603 line:0%
you don't see a lot of people
who are very worried

00:05:37.737 --> 00:05:41.740 line:0%
about the dynamics
of tribal society in Iraq,
or Syria, you know.

00:05:41.907 --> 00:05:44.543
Trump just wants to throw--
you know, bomb-- bomb them

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:46.545
and then think that
we're gonna win that way.

00:05:46.645 --> 00:05:48.681
We have the phrase,
"wag the dog."

00:05:48.948 --> 00:05:52.384
Other presidents have been
accused of starting wars
to distract,

00:05:52.718 --> 00:05:54.720
do you think Trump
is above that?

00:05:55.087 --> 00:05:56.155
ELIOT: No, I-- (STUTTERS)

00:05:56.589 --> 00:05:59.125
MAX: There's almost nothing
that Trump is above,
I would say. (CHUCKLES)

00:05:59.358 --> 00:06:01.928
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)
-BILL: Oh... Geraldo!

00:06:01.994 --> 00:06:04.096
(LAUGHTER AND APPLAUSE)

00:06:04.296 --> 00:06:05.831
BILL: I'll hold him,
you punch him.

00:06:05.898 --> 00:06:07.466
When you say something
like that,

00:06:07.733 --> 00:06:11.403
what you ignore is that
we get one president
at a time.

00:06:12.304 --> 00:06:15.341 line:0%
We get one president--
When he succeeds,
the nation succeeds,

00:06:15.441 --> 00:06:17.610 line:0%
when he fails,
the nation is failing--

00:06:17.743 --> 00:06:19.945 line:0%
-MAX: I'd love to see
him succeed--
-BILL: Yeah, so would I.

00:06:20.045 --> 00:06:23.316
When you alienate yourself
from the government, and say,

00:06:23.516 --> 00:06:26.585
"Nothing they do
is worth a shit,"
then the country--

00:06:26.685 --> 00:06:28.154
BILL: But that's not
what we're doing.

00:06:28.220 --> 00:06:29.221
(OVERLAPPING CHATTER)

00:06:29.722 --> 00:06:31.456
We're not saying we don't want
him to succeed,
what we're saying is that

00:06:31.556 --> 00:06:34.660 line:0%
his absence of fact-based
decision making.

00:06:34.726 --> 00:06:36.229 line:0%
-BILL: Right.
-And as Geraldo
just pointed out--

00:06:36.295 --> 00:06:37.863 line:0%
-(APPLAUSE)
-GERALDO: I'm Geraldo.

00:06:37.930 --> 00:06:39.398 line:0%
(CHUCKLES)
As Bill just pointed out,

00:06:39.464 --> 00:06:41.767 line:0%
the decision to move
the National Guard
to the border,

00:06:41.900 --> 00:06:44.236
I view as a manifestation
of a bad week,

00:06:44.370 --> 00:06:46.372
he wants to distract.
He does something--

00:06:46.439 --> 00:06:47.973
Barack Obama did the same thing!

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:50.142
ELIOT: Yes. No, no, no,
but not in this moment, not--

00:06:50.209 --> 00:06:51.777
George Bush did the same thing!

00:06:51.877 --> 00:06:53.879
(OVERLAPPING CHATTER)

00:06:54.112 --> 00:06:56.415
We all-- We all want him
to succeed, this guy won't.

00:06:56.481 --> 00:06:57.550
BILL: But, by the way--

00:06:57.850 --> 00:06:59.484
GERALDO: When was the last time
you said something nice
about him?

00:06:59.551 --> 00:07:01.887
-BILL: Ask me that. Ask me that.
-ELIOT: Earlier in the show.
Earlier in the show.

00:07:01.954 --> 00:07:03.221
GERALDO:
Okay, when was the last time?

00:07:03.321 --> 00:07:07.292
When he made the--
When Kim Jong-un said, uh,
"Let's meet,"

00:07:07.826 --> 00:07:09.862
and Trump said,
"Great, let's meet."

00:07:10.162 --> 00:07:12.297
-And all the liberals said,
"That's crazy"...
-Great.

00:07:12.431 --> 00:07:14.801
...and I said, "No, you know,
these two guys probably

00:07:14.934 --> 00:07:17.736
are the two craziest people
in the world, they might
understand each other."

00:07:17.803 --> 00:07:18.804
(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:07:18.971 --> 00:07:20.305
-I also supported--
-...Laura Ingraham also.

00:07:20.372 --> 00:07:22.675
I also supported moving
the capital to Jerusalem.

00:07:22.808 --> 00:07:26.512
So, believe me, I am perfectly
capable of agreeing with him--

00:07:26.578 --> 00:07:28.781
I'll give you another one.
Another one that's important,
the tariffs.

00:07:28.948 --> 00:07:30.983
The Democrats should stand up
and say, "You know what,

00:07:31.083 --> 00:07:33.052
it's time we stood up
against China.

00:07:33.118 --> 00:07:36.622
We should do it
as a global coalition,
not as one-off deals."

00:07:36.822 --> 00:07:39.224
Somebody had to stand up,
China was gaming the system.

00:07:39.358 --> 00:07:42.160
Wait a second,
I don't think Democrats
ought to be supporting Trump's

00:07:42.427 --> 00:07:43.996
trying to start a trade war
with China.

00:07:44.096 --> 00:07:45.431
This is not going to
work out well.

00:07:45.631 --> 00:07:48.400
No, but we need to stand up
to China on trade.
It's about time we did it.

00:07:48.467 --> 00:07:51.369
Yeah, but not-- not this way.
Not this blunderbuss approach,
with these massive terms.

00:07:51.436 --> 00:07:52.971
...but we need to stand up.
It's about time
somebody said that.

00:07:53.138 --> 00:07:55.775
Eliot, what do you think about
Republicans deregulating
the banks?

00:07:55.841 --> 00:07:57.776
And some Democrats
deregulating the banks?

00:07:57.877 --> 00:08:01.246
Well, here's the thing I'll say:
It's been so many years since
we had a financial crisis,

00:08:01.313 --> 00:08:03.015
-don't we want one?
-(HEATHER LAUGHS)

00:08:03.082 --> 00:08:05.083
-(GERALDO LAUGHS)
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:08:05.150 --> 00:08:10.088
-GERALDO: Ten years.
-It's the single-most
moronic policy move I've seen

00:08:10.389 --> 00:08:12.658
since moving the National Guard
to the border. It is--

00:08:12.791 --> 00:08:13.959
(LAUGHTER AND APPLAUSE)

00:08:14.259 --> 00:08:17.829
I mean, this is-- (LAUGHS)
The fact that ten years after
the crisis,

00:08:17.996 --> 00:08:21.967
we want to go back
and recreate the very predicate
to the crisis of '08

00:08:22.401 --> 00:08:25.804
just makes no sense.
Banks are lending,
they're lending enough.

00:08:25.904 --> 00:08:27.172
The economy is booming.

00:08:27.406 --> 00:08:30.576
Why go back to minimizing
and limiting the amount
of capital they need?

00:08:30.809 --> 00:08:32.144
It's insane. Simply insane.

00:08:32.311 --> 00:08:33.712
-But it's also--
-(APPLAUSE)

00:08:33.979 --> 00:08:38.316
I completely agree with you.
One of my happiest moments
in Washington D.C.,

00:08:38.383 --> 00:08:41.854 line:0%
they are few,
was when I worked on
the Wall Street Reform Bill.

00:08:42.288 --> 00:08:46.191 line:0%
Sat there at the bill signing,
saw us really try
to turn the page,

00:08:46.325 --> 00:08:50.028 line:0%
from a time when Wall Street
and the banks wrote
all of the rules.

00:08:50.329 --> 00:08:55.834
And the fact is, they still are
the biggest donor
to Democrats and Republicans

00:08:55.901 --> 00:08:58.537
in the financial sector.
And seeing that list
of Democrats

00:08:58.604 --> 00:09:01.207
that Elizabeth Warren
had the guts to call out,

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:05.277
that list of Democrats
who are saying, "You know what,
let's deregulate again.

00:09:05.444 --> 00:09:08.013
-Let's go ahead and join
with the Republican caucus."
-BILL: Right.

00:09:08.213 --> 00:09:12.418
This is why the Democratic Party
is not as popular
as it needs to be

00:09:12.551 --> 00:09:14.553
with working and middle class
people of all races.

00:09:14.720 --> 00:09:16.956
BILL: All right.
Thank you very much, everybody.
Thank you, panel.

00:09:17.089 --> 00:09:19.191
-(APPLAUSE)
-BILL: We did it again.

